# Cursor workflow

- Follow `.cursor/rules/00-project-operating-model.mdc` for delivery flow,
  task levels, role routing, validation policy and educational gates.
- Treat root and path-scoped `AGENTS.md` files as constitutional repository
  instructions (ADRs, freeze decisions, authority matrix).
- Read `HANDOFF.md` before material work; use `.cursor/rules/25-handoff.mdc`
  and skill `session-handoff` for updates.
- Resolve applicable workflows from `planning/skills/skills-registry.yaml`
  and role skills under `.claude/skills/`; do not duplicate skill procedures
  in prompts.
- Use Plan Mode before multi-file architecture, database, migration, security,
  or public-contract work when the change is costly to reverse.
- For independent analysis or the single post-implementation review, prefer
  read-only subagents. The parent agent is the only writer unless the plan
  assigns disjoint files.
- Inspect existing implementation, tests, planning and accepted ADRs before
  proposing changes.
- Do not fabricate human approval. Record unresolved production topics as
  `BLOCKED_FOR_PRODUCTION` without blocking safe local educational work.
- Do not push or execute destructive Git operations unless explicitly
  authorised by the user.
- Before completion: focused verification, one implementation review when
  code changed, update `HANDOFF.md`, then one coherent commit when asked.
